<!-- 01 INTRO -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01, About this service</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Maytag dryers on the Whirlpool platform.</h2>

    <p><strong>When a Maytag dryer fails in an LA home, our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair trace it to a handful of repeat patterns: a blown thermal fuse from a blocked vent (the most common no-heat repair, $145–$245, vent always inspected first); a burned-out heating element ($285–$425, electric MED, year 8–12); a squealing drum belt and idler pulley ($185–$285); and the F22/F23/F31 sensor codes (thermistor or moisture sensor, $145–$215), about 30% of which clear at the connector-reseat or sensor-cleaning step.</strong> Gas MGD models add the igniter and gas valve coil ($245–$385). Maytag runs on the Whirlpool platform, so parts cross-fit with Whirlpool, KitchenAid, and Amana. We service MED, MGD, Bravos, Maxima, and Centennial units across the Valley, the Inland Empire, Pasadena, and the Westside. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited.</p>
    <p class="batch2-info-guides" style="margin:16px 0 0; padding:12px 16px; background:#fafafa; border-left:3px solid #C8102E; border-radius:4px; font-size:0.95rem;"><strong style="color:#666; font-weight:600;">Related diagnostic guides:</strong> <a href="/services/dryer-repair/maytag-not-heating/" style="color:#C8102E; font-weight:600; text-decoration:none;">why your Maytag dryer won't heat</a></p>

    <p>Maytag has been part of Whirlpool Corporation since the 2006 acquisition, with US laundry manufacturing concentrated alongside the Whirlpool platform. The dryer catalog spans three lines: <strong>Bravos</strong> (the brand's premium top-load washer-paired dryers, MED / MGD-X series with steam cycles), <strong>Maxima</strong> (front-load matching dryers, electronic controls), and <strong>Centennial</strong> (entry-tier basic top-load-paired dryers). The "built to last" reputation that Maytag carried for decades was earned on the older Maytag-Newton platform; current production sits on Whirlpool engineering with shared parts, shared diagnostic tree, and parts cross-reference across the entire Whirlpool family.</p>

    <p>For service that's straightforward: Whirlpool F-codes apply directly, our trucks carry components that fit Maytag, Whirlpool, KitchenAid, and Amana with substantial overlap, and most Maytag dryer repairs run efficiently because we already know the platform. <a href="/brands/maytag-washer-repair/">Brand hub</a> covers Maytag's full appliance lineup; this page is dryer-specific.</p>
  </div>
</section>


